From d750b851b1b3ccd7f3d7aff50e6995a5de3733c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kane-Chen-AS <kane_chen@aspeedtech.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 15:05:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] webui-vue: poll TaskMonitor to completion for multipart
 upload

The multipart HTTP push upload previously returned as soon as the
upload request completed, without waiting for the BMC to actually
finish processing the firmware update task. This caused the UI to
show the "verify update" message too early for the multipart path.

Poll the TaskMonitor URI returned in the upload response every 5
seconds (cache disabled to always get a fresh status) until the task
is no longer in the "running" (202) state, up to a 10 minute limit.
Surface a distinct error message when the task monitor itself
reports a failure (500).

FirmwareFormUpdate.vue is updated to only use the old 6-minute
timer-based verify message for the plain httpPush path; for the
multipart path, the verify message is now shown after the task
polling resolves instead.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Kane-Chen-AS <kane_chen@aspeedtech.com>
